KG42.register("clusters-60e4a19e3b334076b8da8cf1",{"id":"03-bilateral_p2p::v142-d-K003","paper":"03-bilateral_p2p","label":"Dual-market participation permission for actors with loads and local renewable resources","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Dual-market participation permission for actors with loads and local renewable resources","market_meaning":"The consuming actors listed in R005 and the actors with local renewable resources covered by R006 may participate in the forward and real-time contract markets. The two chains jointly describe participation permission under resource configurations, retaining their overlapping scopes without thereby establishing mutually exclusive actor categories or universal generation-eligibility requirements.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The two chains fall within the dual-market participation scope of the same mechanism. R005 covers its listed configurations of loads, flexible loads, and/or renewable resources, while R006 retains its narrower scope of configurations with local renewable resources. consumer and prosumer are not treated as synonymous or mutually exclusive in this assembly, nor is local generation elevated to a necessary condition for all prosumer actors in the paper.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The two chains have the same market-participation consequence and supplement the participation scope through overlapping resource configurations, making them suitable for assembly into a participation-permission cluster. Its boundary excludes price-offer, selection, and fulfillment algorithms, and it does not claim to establish an exhaustive eligibility classification.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the main description of permission for consuming actors to participate in the forward and real-time markets under their load and resource characteristics."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Retains participation permission for actors with local renewable resources as a supplement to the same market-participation scope; the portion overlapping with R005 is not counted as an additional independent rule."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e01","v141-b-g01-e09"],"rationale":"The description of consumer resources in the abstract and the prosumer description in the main text both refer to this mechanism's forward and real-time contract markets and overlap in configurations with local renewable resources. This connection assembles only the participation scope, without establishing identity equivalence or a participation dependency between the two actor roles."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"The participation scope relies on unreviewed quotations from the abstract and main text, and the current source status remains unverified. Assembly of the candidate permissions does not signify independent confirmation of the transcriptions or role interpretations.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e01","v141-b-g01-e09"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the two participant descriptions and their applicability to both markets, retaining the nonexclusive meaning of and/or without rewriting descriptive resource combinations as new entry thresholds."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G002","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The main text permits and/or combinations of loads and renewable resources, and the case study also calls actors without PV prosumer; R006 covers only those configurations with local renewable resources. Although the permissions in the two chains overlap, their frozen nodes and constraint scopes cannot be directly identified as the same objects.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::participation.consumer","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R006::V::participation.prosumer","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e01","v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-E23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually confirm the correspondence between the paper's actor categories and the frozen functional roles. If exhaustive coverage of the paper's prosumer scope is needed, have upstream C address R006's scope issue; this round does not merge nodes, deduplicate on the basis of identical expressions, or expand the original permissions."}]},"rule_refs":["03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R005","03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R006"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-a774da994c2ca212","COMP-d3fb5a9d87fcd5a7"]});
